{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-53202","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101599","text":"Agent lanes — what can be worked on in parallel, and what will collide"}]},{"id":"blk-53203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101600","marks":["bold"],"text":"Written 2026-08-15."},{"id":"spn-101601","text":" Six lanes. Each has a brief in this directory. Start a session by pointing it at its brief; the brief is written to be self-sufficient."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101602","marks":["bold"],"text":"2026-08-16 — a second set exists: `agents/SITES.md`, lanes G–N"},{"id":"spn-101603","text":", covering the domain "},{"id":"spn-101604","marks":["code"],"text":"index.html"},{"id":"spn-101605","text":"s. It touches no A–F file. Two things in it bind every lane here too: "},{"id":"spn-101606","marks":["bold"],"text":"half the domains live in `/home/travis/Projects/`, not this tree"},{"id":"spn-101607","text":", and four names exist in both with only one copy live. See "},{"id":"spn-101608","marks":["code"],"text":"SITES.md"},{"id":"spn-101609","text":" §0.1 for the byte-count check that settles which."}]}],"id":"blk-53204","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101610","marks":["bold"],"text":"`docs/` is the stackdocs aggregation site"},{"id":"spn-101611","text":" and anything put there is swept into the atlas build. That is why these live in "},{"id":"spn-101612","marks":["code"],"text":"agents/"},{"id":"spn-101613","text":" at the root instead."}]}],"id":"blk-53206","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-53208","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101614","text":"The constraint that shapes everything: one working tree"}]},{"id":"blk-53209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101615","marks":["bold"],"text":"All your sessions share `/home/travis/ProjectAmp2`. There are no worktrees."},{"id":"spn-101616","text":" Two agents editing the same file is not merge conflict — it is one silently overwriting the other, and it has cost real work before."}]},{"id":"blk-53210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101617","marks":["bold"],"text":"So the lanes are partitioned by file ownership, and the ownership is the contract."},{"id":"spn-101618","text":" Every brief opens with what it owns and what it must not touch. If a lane needs a file another lane owns, it says so and stops rather than reaching across."}]},{"id":"blk-53211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101619","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not run all six at once."},{"id":"spn-101620","text":" Three or four is the realistic ceiling on one tree."}]},{"id":"blk-53212","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101621","text":"Can they start now?"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-53214","spans":[{"id":"spn-101622","text":"Lane"}]},{"id":"blk-53215","spans":[{"id":"spn-101623","text":"Owns"}]},{"id":"blk-53216","spans":[{"id":"spn-101624","text":"Ready?"}]}],"id":"blk-53213","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-53217","spans":[{"id":"spn-101625","marks":["bold"],"text":"A — Shell wiring"}]},{"id":"blk-53218","spans":[{"id":"spn-101626","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/m2/"},{"id":"spn-101627","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101628","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/test/"}]},{"id":"blk-53219","spans":[{"id":"spn-101629","text":"⚠️ "},{"id":"spn-101630","marks":["bold"],"text":"only if no other session is in `m2/`"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53220","spans":[{"id":"spn-101631","marks":["bold"],"text":"B — studbook"}]},{"id":"blk-53221","spans":[{"id":"spn-101632","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook/"}]},{"id":"blk-53222","spans":[{"id":"spn-101633","text":"❌ blocked on two [TRAVIS] rulings"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53223","spans":[{"id":"spn-101634","marks":["bold"],"text":"C — Infrastructure"}]},{"id":"blk-53224","spans":[{"id":"spn-101635","text":"no repo files; cloud accounts"}]},{"id":"blk-53225","spans":[{"id":"spn-101636","text":"❌ needs you present — spend and credentials"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53226","spans":[{"id":"spn-101637","marks":["bold"],"text":"D — Worker / auth / control plane"}]},{"id":"blk-53227","spans":[{"id":"spn-101638","marks":["code"],"text":"worker/"},{"id":"spn-101639","text":", "},{"id":"spn-101640","marks":["bold"],"text":"incl. `worker/migrations/`"}]},{"id":"blk-53228","spans":[{"id":"spn-101641","text":"⚠️ "},{"id":"spn-101642","marks":["bold"],"text":"schema + RLS + token tests unblocked 2026-08-21"},{"id":"spn-101643","text":"; cloud integration still on C"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53229","spans":[{"id":"spn-101644","marks":["bold"],"text":"E — Site"}]},{"id":"blk-53230","spans":[{"id":"spn-101645","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven.com/"},{"id":"spn-101646","text":" "},{"id":"spn-101647","marks":["italic"],"text":"(nav moved to lane N, 2026-08-16)"}]},{"id":"blk-53231","spans":[{"id":"spn-101648","text":"✅ "},{"id":"spn-101649","marks":["bold"],"text":"now"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53232","spans":[{"id":"spn-101650","marks":["bold"],"text":"F — Docs reconciliation"}]},{"id":"blk-53233","spans":[{"id":"spn-101651","text":"root "},{"id":"spn-101652","marks":["code"],"text":"*.md"}]},{"id":"blk-53234","spans":[{"id":"spn-101653","text":"✅ "},{"id":"spn-101654","marks":["bold"],"text":"now"}]}],[{"id":"blk-53235","spans":[{"id":"spn-101655","marks":["bold"],"text":"O — Cloud site"}]},{"id":"blk-53236","spans":[{"id":"spn-101656","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud.computedriven.com/"},{"id":"spn-101657","text":" (new, 2026-08-21)"}]},{"id":"blk-53237","spans":[{"id":"spn-101658","text":"✅ "},{"id":"spn-101659","marks":["bold"],"text":"now"},{"id":"spn-101660","text":" — static; its claims read from "},{"id":"spn-101661","marks":["code"],"text":"status.json"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-53238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101662","marks":["bold"],"text":"Start today: D, E, F and O."},{"id":"spn-101663","text":" D's local half needs no cloud account at all — a local Postgres and a locally generated keypair carry the schema, the tenant-isolation battery and token verification."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101664","marks":["bold"],"text":"2026-08-21 — lanes D and O both touch the Cloud v1 round and must not be run in one session."},{"id":"spn-101665","text":" D owns the Worker and the schema; O owns the marketing/status surface. The seam between them is "},{"id":"spn-101666","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud.computedriven.com/status.json"},{"id":"spn-101667","text":", which "},{"id":"spn-101668","marks":["bold"],"text":"O owns and D only reads"},{"id":"spn-101669","text":". If a capability's rung changes, D reports it and O edits the file — never both."}]}],"id":"blk-53239","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-53241","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101670","marks":["bold"],"text":"A is the highest-value build work"},{"id":"spn-101671","text":" and the only question is whether the tracks/reel session is still live. Check "},{"id":"spn-101672","marks":["code"],"text":"git log --oneline -3"},{"id":"spn-101673","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-101674","marks":["code"],"text":"RRABBIT/"},{"id":"spn-101675","text":" — if the newest commit is "},{"id":"spn-101676","marks":["code"],"text":"a4ea112"},{"id":"spn-101677","text":" (\"Somewhere to put a track…\"), that was this session and the lane is free."}]},{"id":"blk-53242","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101678","text":"What is blocking B, C and D — all of it is yours"}]},{"id":"blk-53243","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101679","text":"None of these is a task. Each is a decision only you make."}]},{"id":"blk-53244","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101680","marks":["bold"],"text":"studbook §10.5 — does the identity ladder admit a `track-` prefix?"},{"id":"spn-101681","text":" A track records a *live OS"}]}],"id":"blk-53245","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-53247","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101682","text":"world*, not a sealed "},{"id":"spn-101683","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-101684","text":" world. The code already uses "},{"id":"spn-101685","marks":["code"],"text":"track-"},{"id":"spn-101686","text":" and marks it "},{"id":"spn-101687","marks":["bold"],"text":"provisional"},{"id":"spn-101688","text":"; if the answer is no, that constant changes and every id changes with it. "},{"id":"spn-101689","marks":["bold"],"text":"Blocks B, and makes anything published before it disposable."}]},{"id":"blk-53248","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101690","marks":["bold"],"text":"The index question"},{"id":"spn-101691","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-101692","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFIDENTIALITY.md"},{"id":"spn-101693","text":" §4) — the operator-visible graph: accept it,"}]}],"id":"blk-53249","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-53251","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101694","text":"minimise it, or encrypt it. Recommendation is "},{"id":"spn-101695","marks":["italic"],"text":"minimise"},{"id":"spn-101696","text":" (ids, sizes, edges; no names, no paths). "},{"id":"spn-101697","marks":["bold"],"text":"Blocks B's schema."}]},{"id":"blk-53252","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101698","marks":["bold"],"text":"The threat model"},{"id":"spn-101699","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-101700","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFIDENTIALITY.md"},{"id":"spn-101701","text":" §1) — which of T1–T7 are in scope. Everything in"}]}],"id":"blk-53253","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-53255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101702","text":"class B (private data) is downstream. "},{"id":"spn-101703","marks":["bold"],"text":"Blocks B's crypto, not its index."}]},{"id":"blk-53256","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-53258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101704","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spend approval"},{"id":"spn-101705","text":" for Hetzner, Fly, PlanetScale, Cloudflare R2. "},{"id":"sp